Package: UiOPregnancyAlgorithm
Type: Package
Title: UiO Pregnancy Algorithm for the Norwegian Health Registries
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Hedvig M. E.", "Nordeng", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6361-2918")),
    person("Saeed", "Hayati", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "saeedha@uio.no"),
    person("Marleen M. H. J.", "van Gelder", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4853-4434")))
Description: Identifies pregnancies, their outcomes (live birth, stillbirth, miscarriage,
    induced abortion, molar and ectopic pregnancy) and their start dates in the Medical Birth
    Registry of Norway (MBRN), the Norwegian Patient Registry (NPR) and the primary-care claims
    database (KUHR), with the UiO pregnancy algorithm described in Nordeng et al. (2024)
    <doi:10.1002/pds.70002>. The algorithm is an R translation of the STATA script by
    M. M. H. J. van Gelder. Its rules (stillbirth limit and birth weight, the marker rule, the
    look-back for pregnancy markers, the gap that separates events, the default pregnancy
    lengths) are arguments, and the settings of version 1.3 can be restored.
    Experimental: MBRN single births without gestational age are kept with an imputed gestational age
    (experimental), and run_uio_pa() writes a report on these records.
